($q$Eiffel Excellence Scholarship Programme$q$,$q$French Ministry for Europe and Foreign Affairs (run by Campus France)$q$,$q$France$q$,$q$Not stated$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$For foreign students under 29 (Master's) or under 35 (PhD), in priority fields. Only French higher education institutions can submit applications, so apply through the institution you want to join. No excluded countries are listed on the page.$q$,'2027-01-06'::date,$q$https://campusfrance.org/en/eiffel-scholarship-program-of-excellence$q$,$q$Benefits not described on the page$q$),
($q$Erasmus Mundus Joint Masters Scholarships$q$,$q$European Commission (Erasmus+)$q$,$q$Europe (several countries)$q$,$q$Full$q$,$q$Postgraduate$q$,$q$Students from all over the world with a Bachelor's degree (or in final year) can apply directly to a joint Master's programme run by universities in at least two European countries. Check each programme for its deadline.$q$,NULL::date,$q$https://erasmus-plus.ec.europa.eu/opportunities/individuals/students/erasmus-mundus-joint-masters$q$,$q$Covers participation costs, with a contribution to travel, visa and living allowance for awarded students$q$),
